**Why the platform never finished loading**

1. `node_modules/@tailwindcss/oxide-win32-x64-msvc` (Tailwind's native binary) was missing, so `globals.css` failed to compile and *every* route returned 500. I fetched the exact 4.3.3 build into `node_modules` without touching `package.json`, then restarted the dev server.
2. `src/app/posts/[slug]/loading.tsx` (a full-screen spinner) put the whole article behind a streamed boundary that only got revealed by a `requestAnimationFrame` callback. When that callback is delayed (background tab, throttled paint), the article stayed hidden behind "Loading post" indefinitely. Removed it plus its `en`/`fr`/`ar` re-exports — the article now arrives inline in the first HTML response (`/en/posts/t` → h1 present in raw markup, no `Loading post`).
3. The stored post HTML is pretty-printed, so newlines between `<table>`/`<thead>`/`<tr>` tags became real text nodes → React hydration errors on every post with a table, which broke interactivity. Non-whitespace text nodes inside table containers are now dropped in [rich-article-content.tsx](src/app/components/rich-article-content.tsx).

**Post-view work you asked for**

- **Table of contents** — [article-toc.tsx](src/app/posts/%5Bslug%5D/article-toc.tsx): a small dark/yellow circular list icon floats bottom-right; it opens a panel of every `h2`/`h3`, highlights the section you're reading, closes on link click, Escape or outside click, and uses the localised heading label (added for en/fr/ar in [i18n.ts](src/lib/i18n.ts)).
- **Heading anchors** — every `h2`/`h3` now gets a stable, de-duplicated id (`#setting-up-the-project`, …) with scroll offset, so contents links and shared URLs land correctly.
- **Link colour** — links are now olive-gold `#6f5a00` text on a 2px `#f2d600` underline, filling with a 30% yellow highlight on hover, matching the site's yellow accent instead of washing out on white.
- **Code blocks, Stack Overflow style** — light `#f6f6f6` card, `#d6d9dc` hairline border, 13px monospace at 1.65 line-height and `tab-size: 4`; inline code uses the same `#eff0f1` chip.
- **Images** — [globals.css](src/app/globals.css) `article-image`: on hover a 1.2% lift, soft shadow, slight saturation bump and a yellow outline, disabled under `prefers-reduced-motion`.

**Checks run:** `tsc --noEmit` clean, `next build` succeeded, `/en`, `/en/posts/t` and the microservices post all 200, and in the browser I confirmed 16 TOC entries with correct anchors, the panel opening/closing, computed code-block styles (`rgb(246,246,246)` / `rgb(214,217,220)` / 13px mono) and the image hover rule live. The preview browser tab can't paint (its animation frames are throttled), so smooth-scroll and the active-section highlight were verified structurally rather than by watching them; they'll behave normally in your own window. Dev server is running on 3000 and registered in the Preview tab.

The obvious next step is checking the same fix on the other locale post routes and the admin pages that render tables.
